# Files that guard production. A change to any of them needs the owner's
# review before it can merge into `dev` or `main` — once the branch ruleset
# requires code-owner review (docs/RUNBOOK-agent-controls.md, step 2). Until
# then this file only requests the review; it does not enforce it.
#
# Later rules win, so keep the list flat: one path, one owner.
#
# Adding a guard, a gate test or a security file? Add its path here in the
# same PR (docs/compliance/information-security-program.md, §3). A pattern
# that matches nothing yet is harmless: GitHub ignores it until the file lands.

